The error "InvalidLocationConstraint: The specified location-constraint is not valid" typically occurs when you're trying to create an S3 bucket in a region that doesn't support bucket creation, or when you're not specifying a region at all.

In your code, you're not specifying a region for the bucket. When you create a bucket, you need to specify a region where the bucket will reside. Here's how you can modify your code to specify a region:

```javascript
await s3.createBucket({
  Bucket: s3Bucket,
  ACL: 'public-read',
  CreateBucketConfiguration: {
    LocationConstraint: 'us-west-2' // specify your desired region here
  }
}).promise();
```

In the above code, replace `'us-west-2'` with the AWS region you want to use. You can find a list of all AWS regions and their corresponding codes here: https://docs.aws.amazon.com/general/latest/gr/rande.html

If you don't specify a region, the bucket will be created in the S3 region that your client is located in, which might not be the region you intended.

